# [M5.0] D27 axis 4 -- \p{...}/\P{...} general categories (extract Sec 3.1/3.4).
# 37 accepted spellings (7 one-letter + 30 two-letter) x 2 polarities x 2
# (member-focus / non-member-focus blocks) = 148 blocks (the extract's own
# "148, rounded" -> 150; this generator delivers the exact 148, not the
# rounded figure -- see REPORT.md), 4 subjects each -> 592 future cases.
# Every block `perr`s today (LIVE-verified): \p is gated on the
# 'unicode-props' module regardless of `--features` or encoding.
#
# Membership is MEASURED against a ~37-candidate code-point pool via
# `^\p{XX}$` under PCRE2_UTF -- never assumed from a hand-written category
# table. \p{Cs} (surrogates) structurally has zero reachable pool members: a
# surrogate scalar has no valid UTF-8 encoding, so every subject in its two
# blocks is (correctly) a non-member; that absence IS the measurement.

